    <briefdescription>
<para>An array operand of a comparator, other than a <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> array. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparators convert the arrays of any element type except <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> (the byte buffers, the arrays of numbers, and the arrays of the wide character types) to this type (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>), so that they are compared element by element, and written as ranges, instead of being compared and written as the addresses they decay to. Two arrays of different sizes are never equal.</para>
<para>The elements are not copied; the operand must outlive the comparison, which is always the case within a check.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The element type, possibly <computeroutput>const</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
